        Chapter 4: General Notes                                        4-1









                             CHAPTER 4 - General Notes




              * The limit on the number of buckets to 20000  decimal  is  a
                restriction imposed by these utilities, not by the  system.
                AOS/VS requires  that  the  utility  be  resident  for  the
                duration of the histogram, and  the  pages  containing  the
                buckets counters are implicitly wired into  memory  by  the
                system during the processing of ?WHIST.  As a  result,  the
                bucket counter pages will neither swap out  nor  page  out,
                increasing system memory  contention.   Additional  buckets
                were   determined   to   unnecessarily   penalize    system
                performance.

              * There is no limit on the size of the buckets.  Buckets  may
                cross ring  boundaries.   Also,  the  buckets  may  contain
                addresses invalid to the target process.

              * Histograms may be run from the very initialization  of  the
                target process.  This is accomplished by  issuing  a  ?PROC
                with the ?PFBS flag set; this will cause the target  to  be
                blocked immediately after it is created.  A  histogram  may
                then be activated and the target unblocked.  The  immediate
                blocking of the target may also be accomplished through the
                CLI utility by specifying the switch /BSON on  the  PROCESS
                command.



                                 [End of Chapter 4]

















        Data General Corporation                       Company Confidential
        
